cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or reference this interactive 3D spatial edition of Vitruvius' De Architectura, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Vitruvius — The City of the Ten Books: An Interactive 3D Spatial & Bilingual Edition of De Architectura"
authors:
  - family-names: "Poturak"
    given-names: "Semir"
    name-suffix: "PhD"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-11"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - "Vitruvius"
  - "De Architectura"
  - "Ten Books on Architecture"
  - "Architectural History"
  - "Digital Humanities"
  - "3D Spatial Humanities"
  - "Classical Architecture"
abstract: >-
  An interactive 3D architectural atlas and bilingual scholarly edition of Marcus Vitruvius Pollio's
  De Architectura (Books I–X), mapping all 729 passages of M. H. Morgan's 1914 Harvard University Press
  English translation (pp. 3–319) alongside F. Krohn's 1912 Teubner Latin text onto 261 procedurally
  constructed 3D architectural monuments governed by 132 verbatim Vitruvian geometric rules.
